atment of unselected patients with coronary artery disease</article-title><source>Chin Med J (Engl)</source><year>2006</year><volume>119</volume><fpage>165</fpage><lpage>168</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16455001</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Weisz</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Leon</surname><given-names>MB</given-names></name><name><surname>Holmes</surname><given-names>DR</given-names><suffix>Jr</suffix></name><name><surname>Kereiakes</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Clark</surname><given-names>MR</given-names></name><name><surname>Cohen</surname><given-names>BM</given-names></name><name><surname>Ellis</surname><given-names>SG</given-names></name><name><surname>Coleman</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Hill</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Shi</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Cutlip</surname><given-names>DE</given-names></name><name><surname>Kuntz</surname><given-names>RE</given-names></name><name><surname>Moses</surname><given-names>JW</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Two-year outcomes after sirolimus-eluting stent implantation: results from the Sirolimus-Eluting Stent in de Novo Native Coronary Lesions (SIRIUS) trial</article-title><source>J Am Coll Cardiol</source><year>2006</year><volume>47</volume><fpage>1350</fpage><lpage>1355</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16580520</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.jacc.2005.11.077</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Flaherty</surname><given-names>JDDC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Diabetes and coronary revascularization</article-title><source>JAMA</source><year>2005</year><volume>293</volume><fpage>1501</fpage><lpage>1508</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmi